# 301 redirects from old domain to new domain.
# Covers both protocols (http/https) and www/non-www variants.
# The `!` at the end forces the redirect even if a matching file exists.
# :splat captures the wildcard path so /projects/comi-app, etc. all redirect to the same page on the new domain.

http://beniyorohan-design.com/*       https://beniyorohan.design/:splat  301!
https://beniyorohan-design.com/*      https://beniyorohan.design/:splat  301!
http://www.beniyorohan-design.com/*   https://beniyorohan.design/:splat  301!
https://www.beniyorohan-design.com/*  https://beniyorohan.design/:splat  301!

# Client tools live on their own subdomain: tools.beniyorohan.design (a domain alias of this site).
# /lous = the Lou's Fancy Foods asset generator (files in /lff-tool/). Anything else on the
# tools host goes back to the portfolio, so the subdomain never mirrors the whole site.
# (Netlify matches /lous and /lous/ alike, so both serve the page; the page itself adds the
# trailing slash so its relative files load from /lous/.)
https://tools.beniyorohan.design/lous     /lff-tool/index.html                    200!
https://tools.beniyorohan.design/lous/*   /lff-tool/:splat                        200!
http://tools.beniyorohan.design/*         https://tools.beniyorohan.design/:splat 301!
https://tools.beniyorohan.design/*        https://beniyorohan.design/             302!
